What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_distance_crosstalk
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Crosstalk compensation of the VL53L1X, in counts per second
		per SPAD. Crosstalk is light that goes back to the sensor
		without a target, for example the reflection of a cover
		window. The sensor removes this part of the signal before it
		calculates the distance. 0 turns the compensation off.

		The value is lost when the sensor is reset. User space can
		store it and write it again after a reset.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_distance_crosstalk_calibrate
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Writing starts a crosstalk calibration. The driver averages
		50 ranging results and then sets in_distance_crosstalk.

		Write 0 when there is no target in the range of the sensor.
		Then all of the signal is crosstalk. Or write the distance in
		millimeters of a target in front of the sensor. The write
		returns when the calibration is complete.
